{"author":{"id":"5698b6d16d951325374257d86a2e673da0e55970c3d21c0f7c6f49018f24e5bf"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1786969081,"nonce":"c2okkTjc97+rOdRxaA/RgyRNFbI=","title":"There is no way to put decorative ink on a surface: no wash token, no mask utility, and nothing that hides it under forced colors","message":"The brand sheet's brush exists as two inlined logo components and nothing else. `Wordmark.tsx` and `Logo.tsx` are `currentColor` SVG elements, which is correct for a mark that sits in the DOM as content — and useless for decoration, because a decorative stroke has to sit *behind* or *beside* something without occupying a slot in the layout. Every motif in the design study resolved to the same shape: a CSS mask over a Tier-A token fill. There is currently no token for that fill, no utility for the mask, and no guard for what the mask does under forced colors.\n\n**The demonstration.** Grep `web/src` for `mask-image` and there are no hits. Grep for a decorative colour token and there are none: `tokens.css` publishes surfaces, borders, four text levels, the accent and the six state quads, all of which are load-bearing and none of which is \"ink that means nothing\". A component that wants a faint stroke today has exactly two options — a hardcoded `rgba()`, which `TestNoStateHueInChrome` does not catch because it is not a state hue and which breaks the moment the theme flips, or an `\u003cimg\u003e`, which cannot take `currentColor` and therefore needs one file per theme.\n\n**Why it matters.** Four motifs are queued behind this and they are all the same three lines of CSS: the ensō on the door, the two-pass swipe behind a page heading, the kumo form on a quiet state, the sakura petal on `expired`. Landing them independently means four hardcoded tints that drift apart, or one primitive that cannot. The primitive also carries the accessibility contract, which is not optional and is easy to omit per-call-site: decorative ink is exempt from WCAG 1.4.3 and 1.4.11 only for as long as it is genuinely decorative, which means `aria-hidden`, `pointer-events: none`, and — the one everybody misses — `display: none` under `forced-colors: active`, where the OS overrides the tint to a system colour at full strength and a 6% wash becomes an opaque slab across the panel.\n\nTwo details are worth writing into the primitive rather than discovering per-motif. The token must be **derived, not themed**: `color-mix(in oklab, var(--oto-text) 6%, transparent)` in the bare `:root` block inherits `--oto-text` and is therefore correct in both palettes from one declaration. That placement is also what keeps it out of `tokens.test.ts`, which reads only rules whose prelude names a theme (`tokens.css:191-198` says so about the type steps), and out of `contrast.test.ts`, which wants a measured pair for every token in §M.4/§M.5 — a decorative wash has no contrast obligation to measure, which is precisely why it must not sit in a palette block. And every stretched motif asset must carry `preserveAspectRatio=\"none\"` **in the SVG itself**: the default `xMidYMid meet` letterboxes the art inside the mask box and the mask goes transparent at the edges, which does not present as a scaling bug — it presents as the content having vanished.\n\n**Where.** `web/src/design/tokens.css:173-178` (the non-themed `:root` block where `--oto-row-h` lives, and where the wash belongs), `:191-198` (the comment stating why non-themed values sit outside `[data-theme]`), `:200-233` (the type/radius/spacing block, the other resident); `web/src/index.css:150-159` (the `@utility`-not-`@layer` convention and why), `:164`, `:178`, `:218`, `:239` (the four existing `@utility` declarations to match); `web/src/index.css.test.ts` (fails the build if a first-party utility is not declared with `@utility`); `web/src/design/tokens.test.ts` and `web/src/design/contrast.test.ts` (the two gates the placement is chosen to satisfy); `web/public/` (currently one 0-byte `.gitkeep` — masks need a URL, so this is where the motif SVGs land, and it stops being the kind of empty directory ticket `d6d97de` was filed about).\n\n**Scope.** small — one derived token, one `@utility`, one directory. It is first only because four motifs are behind it.\n\n**Done when.** `--oto-wash` exists in the non-themed `:root` block, derived from `--oto-text` so both palettes are correct from one declaration, and `tokens.test.ts` and `contrast.test.ts` both stay green without being taught about it. A registered `@utility` applies the mask fill, `pointer-events: none`, `user-select: none` and the `forced-colors: active` guard in one place, so no call site can take the ink without the guard. `web/public/motifs/` holds the assets, every stretched one carries `preserveAspectRatio=\"none\"`, and the reason is written next to them rather than rediscovered. Nothing in `web/src` uses a hardcoded `rgba()` for decorative ink.","files":null}]}